# Highly efficient inverted polymer solar cells by using solution processed MgO/ZnO composite interfacial layers

Shuai Huang a,b, Bonan Kang c, Lan Duan a,b,∗, Dongdong Zhang a,b,∗

a Key Lab of Organic Optoelectronics and Molecular Engineering of Ministry of Education, Department of Chemistry, Tsinghua University, Beijing 100084, China b Center of Flexible Electronics Technology, Tsinghua University, Beijing 100084, China c State Key Laboratory on Integrated Optoelectronics, College of Electronic Science and Engineering, Jilin University, 2699 Qianjin Street, Changchun 130012, China

# g r a p h i c a l a b s t r a c t

The performance of inverted PSC devices based on the PTB7-Th: \(\mathsf{P C}_{71}\mathsf{B M}\) photoactive layer system has been significantly improved by incorporating the \(\mathsf{M g O}/\mathsf{Z n O}\) stacked films with excellent dual-function interface characteristics.

