\[
J=\frac{9}{8}\hat{c}_0\varepsilon_r\mu\left(\frac{V^2}{d^3}\right)
\]

here, \(\varepsilon_{r}\) represents the relative permittivity, \(d\) refers to the thickness of the photoactive layer, \(J\) stands for the current density, \(V\) denotes the effective voltage, \(\varepsilon_{r}\) stands for the dielectric constant of free space, and \(\mu\) refers to zero-field mobility. As displayed in Fig. 8, the electron mobility of the devices are \(9.51\,\times\,10^{-6}\,\,\mathrm{cm}^{2}\,\,\mathrm{V}^{-1}\,\,\mathrm{s}^{-1}\)

